NASA CLD (1:10–1:15) 0.54–0.63 0.59

At CLD ratios, the catalog inclusion criterion rejects three peripheral subsystems due to insufficient NRE recovery, reducing attainable CW-DCI further.

Learning-rate sensitivity. Varying LR across published ranges changes N^* by approximately \pm 6 modules, or \pm 3.5\%. The dominant uncertainty is in avionics and propulsion learning rates.

Standardization ceiling confirmation. Peripheral classes exhibit \sigma_i^{\max} \ge 0.75 with parametric extension; core classes are bounded below \sigma_i^{\max} \le 0.35. The Monte Carlo results confirm this split is robust.

