11. Empirical Validation and Source Audit

This section identifies the critical empirical claims requiring source verification before the work can be considered publication-ready. All values are literature-derived; no original experimental data are presented.

11.1 iSSI Interface Data

The chapter uses specific contemporary claims: LizzieSat-3 flight timing, 0.90 kg interface mass, 1.2 kW power throughput, 24° angular tolerance, 0.5 W/K thermal conductance, TRL 7, and adoption by NASA ARMADAS and commercial stations. Each value requires a directly traceable source rather than a general consortium citation. The iSSI engineering model mass of 0.90 kg should be verified against the flight unit mass data released after March 2025.

11.2 Propulsion System Specifications

