Appendix C: Fault-Tree Analysis Details

C.1 Methodology

Fault-tree analysis (FTA) is used to evaluate the risk implications of functional consolidation. The method proceeds as follows:

1. Define the top event (undesired outcome).
2. Identify intermediate events contributing to the top event.
3. Decompose intermediate events into basic events (component failures).
4. Connect events via AND/OR gates representing logical relationships.
5. Compute top-event probability from basic-event probabilities.
6. Apply phase-dependent criticality weights.

Basic-event failure probabilities use exponential failure models:

P(e) = 1 - \exp(-\lambda_e t),

where \lambda_e is the failure rate from MIL-HDBK-217F or NPRD-2016 and t = 5 years is the mission duration.

